---
import SiteHeader from './SiteHeader.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';

interface Props { locale?: 'en' | 'es'; }
const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const isSpanish = locale === 'es';
const unixInstall = 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DeMaarco/gxx/main/install.sh | sh';
const windowsInstall = 'irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DeMaarco/gxx/main/install.ps1 | iex';
const title = 'gxx — The agent that works where your code lives';
const description = 'A terminal-first coding agent for one workspace. Ask, plan, read, edit, and run with OpenAI or Claude.';
const jsonLd = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'SoftwareApplication', name: 'gxx', applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication', operatingSystem: 'macOS, Linux, Windows', license: 'https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0', codeRepository: 'https://github.com/DeMaarco/gxx', description };
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang={isSpanish ? 'es' : 'en'}>
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#050708" />
		<meta name="description" content={description} />
		<meta name="keywords" content="AI coding agent, terminal coding agent, CLI coding assistant, open source coding agent, developer agent, OpenAI coding agent, Claude coding agent, AI terminal tool" />
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:url" content="https://demaarco.github.io/gxx/" />
		<meta property="og:image" content={`${base}images/hero/hero-core.svg`} />
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<link rel="canonical" href="https://demaarco.github.io/gxx/" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)}></script>
		<title>{title}</title>
	</head>
	<body class="landing-page" data-base={base}>
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
		<div class="preloader" data-preloader aria-hidden="true"><div class="preloader__inner"><span class="eyebrow">INITIALIZING GXX</span><div class="preloader__bar"><span></span></div><div class="preloader__steps"><span>LOAD CORE</span><span>LOAD SCENE</span><span>LOAD WORKSPACE</span></div></div></div>
		<SiteHeader locale={locale} current="home" />
		<div class="cursor-orb" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="scroll-progress" data-scroll-progress aria-hidden="true"></div>

		<main id="main-content">
			<section class="hero section-grid" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
				<div class="hero__art" aria-hidden="true" style={`--art-image: url("${base}images/hero/hero-core.svg")`}><div class="hero__canvas" data-three-scene="hero" data-asset={`${base}models/gxx-core-module.glb`}></div><div class="hero__scanlines"></div><div class="hero__label hero__label--top">GXX / CORE_01 <span class="pulse-dot"></span></div><div class="hero__label hero__label--bottom">WORKSPACE BOUNDARY / LOCAL</div><div class="hero__telemetry mono"><span>ROTATION</span><b>ACTIVE</b><span>FIELD</span><b>ACTIVE</b></div><div class="hero__orbit hero__orbit--one"></div><div class="hero__orbit hero__orbit--two"></div></div>
				<div class="hero__content shell"><div class="hero__copy reveal"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__line"></span>TERMINAL-FIRST / WORKSPACE-AWARE</div><h1 id="hero-title">Your codebase.<br /><em>Your terminal.</em><br />Your agent.</h1><p class="hero__lede">gxx is an open source coding agent that works where your code lives. Open one folder, speak naturally, and keep the boundary, model, and permissions visible.</p><div class="hero__actions"><a class="button button--primary magnetic" href="#install"><span>INSTALL GXX</span><span class="button__arrow">↘</span></a><a class="button button--ghost" href="https://github.com/DeMaarco/gxx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>VIEW ON GITHUB</span><span class="button__arrow">↗</span></a></div><div class="hero__facts mono"><span>OPEN SOURCE</span><i></i><span>APACHE 2.0</span><i></i><span>OPENAI / CLAUDE</span><i></i><span>SSH-READY TERMINAL</span></div></div></div>
				<div class="hero__flow shell" aria-label="gxx architecture flow"><div class="flow-pill"><span class="flow-pill__node">01</span><span>USER</span></div><span class="flow-arrow">↓</span><div class="flow-pill flow-pill--active"><span class="flow-pill__node">02</span><span>TERMINAL</span></div><span class="flow-arrow">↓</span><div class="flow-pill"><span class="flow-pill__node">03</span><span>GXX AGENT</span></div><span class="flow-arrow">↓</span><div class="flow-pill"><span class="flow-pill__node">04</span><span>WORKSPACE</span></div></div>
			</section>

			<section class="signal-strip" aria-label="gxx principles"><div class="shell signal-strip__inner"><span>ONE FOLDER SCOPE</span><span>PLAIN LANGUAGE</span><span>READ / PATCH / RUN</span><span>CONTEXT AWARE</span><span>COST VISIBLE</span></div></section>

			<section class="manifesto section-grid section-space" id="why" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title"><div class="shell manifesto__grid"><div class="section-index mono">/ 01 — THE PREMISE</div><div class="manifesto__content reveal"><h2 id="manifesto-title">Stay close<br /><span>to the code.</span></h2><p>Most of the useful context is already in the project you opened. gxx starts there, keeps its tools inside that workspace, and lets the terminal remain the interface.</p><a class="text-link" href="#workspace">See the workspace boundary <span>→</span></a></div><div class="manifesto__aside mono"><span class="aside-marker">[ LOCAL / 01 ]</span><span>NO DASHBOARD</span><span>NO SECOND SURFACE</span><span>JUST THE PROJECT</span></div></div></section>

			<section class="terminal-section section-space" id="terminal" aria-labelledby="terminal-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 02 — THE LOOP</div><div><p class="eyebrow">A REQUEST BECOMES A WORKFLOW</p><h2 id="terminal-title">One prompt.<br /><em>Real project state.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">No full-screen TUI. A prompt, a status line, and the tools needed to move through a codebase.</p></div><div class="terminal-stage reveal"><div class="terminal-window" data-terminal><div class="terminal-window__top"><div class="terminal-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span class="mono">gxx / my-project</span><span class="terminal-live mono"><b></b> LIVE SESSION</span></div><div class="terminal-window__body"><div class="terminal-line terminal-line--muted mono">~/my-project <span>·</span> gxx v0.0.25</div><div class="terminal-prompt mono"><span class="terminal-caret">&gt;</span><span data-terminal-prompt>explain this repository</span><span class="caret-block"></span></div><div class="terminal-response" data-terminal-response><div class="terminal-step"><span class="step-state">01</span><span>Scanning workspace...</span><b>done</b></div><div class="terminal-step"><span class="step-state">02</span><span>Inspecting files...</span><b>done</b></div><div class="terminal-step"><span class="step-state">03</span><span>Checking git...</span><b>done</b></div><div class="terminal-step terminal-step--active"><span class="step-state">04</span><span>Building context<span class="blink-dots">...</span></span><b>active</b></div><p class="terminal-answer">This project is a Go CLI. The entrypoint is <code>cmd/gxx</code>; tools stay inside this workspace, and the current session is in <span class="tone-cyan">ask</span> mode.</p></div><div class="terminal-status mono"><span>gpt-5.6-sol</span><span class="status-sep">·</span><span class="tone-red">ask</span><span class="status-sep">·</span><span>medium</span><span class="status-sep">·</span><span>272k</span><span class="status-sep">·</span><span class="tone-cyan">context aware</span></div></div></div><div class="terminal-stage__meta mono"><span>SESSION 0001</span><span>READ-ONLY PREVIEW</span><span>EST. COST / SHOWN AFTER TURN</span></div></div><div class="capability-ribbon"><span><b>ASK</b> questions only</span><span><b>PLAN</b> decide before touching</span><span><b>AGENT</b> edits + commands</span><span><b>SKILLS</b> load instructions when relevant</span></div></div></section>

			<section class="modes-section section-space section-grid" id="modes" aria-labelledby="modes-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading section-heading--split reveal"><div><div class="section-index mono">/ 03 — MODES + CONTROL</div><p class="eyebrow">ONE KEY / THREE WAYS TO THINK</p><h2 id="modes-title">Choose the<br /><em>kind of help.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">Ask and Plan are read-only sessions. Agent can apply the work that you approve, according to your permission mode.</p></div><div class="mode-console reveal" data-mode-console><div class="mode-console__nav" role="tablist" aria-label="gxx session modes"><button class="mode-tab is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-mode="ask">ASK <small>READ ONLY</small></button><button class="mode-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mode="plan">PLAN <small>DECIDE FIRST</small></button><button class="mode-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mode="agent">AGENT <small>DO THE WORK</small></button></div><div class="mode-console__body"><div class="mode-visual" data-mode-visual="ask"><div class="mode-ring"></div><div class="mode-core"><span>GXX</span><b>ASK</b></div><div class="mode-orbit mode-orbit--a"><i>READ</i><i>SEARCH</i><i>GIT</i></div><div class="mode-annotation mono">WRITE TOOLS / OFF<br />SHELL / OFF</div></div><div class="mode-copy"><span class="mono mode-number">MODE / <b data-mode-number>01</b></span><h3 data-mode-title>Ask before acting.</h3><p data-mode-copy>Inspect files, search symbols, read git state, and get an answer without changing the project.</p><div class="mode-actions mono"><span data-mode-chip>READ-ONLY TOOLS</span><span>SHIFT+TAB</span></div></div></div></div><div class="permission-console reveal" data-permission-console><div class="permission-console__intro"><span class="eyebrow">AGENT PERMISSION</span><h3>Control the hand<br />that moves.</h3><p>Reads always run. In agent mode, files and shell follow the selected policy.</p></div><div class="permission-console__controls"><div class="segmented" role="tablist" aria-label="permission modes"><button class="permission-tab is-active" data-permission="ask">ASK</button><button class="permission-tab" data-permission="auto-writes">AUTO-WRITES</button><button class="permission-tab" data-permission="auto">AUTO</button></div><div class="permission-grid"><div class="permission-item"><span class="permission-icon">⌁</span><div><b>FILES</b><p data-permission-files>Preview + confirm changes</p></div></div><div class="permission-item"><span class="permission-icon">›_</span><div><b>SHELL</b><p data-permission-shell>Preview + approval menu</p></div></div></div><div class="permission-note mono" data-permission-note>DEFAULT / DENY UNLESS YOU APPROVE</div></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="workspace-section section-space" id="workspace" aria-labelledby="workspace-title"><div class="shell"><div class="workspace-intro"><div class="section-index mono">/ 04 — WORKSPACE AWARE</div><div class="workspace-intro__copy reveal"><p class="eyebrow">ONE FOLDER. ONE REAL BOUNDARY.</p><h2 id="workspace-title">The project<br /><em>is the interface.</em></h2><p>Start gxx inside a directory. That root is the world: files, search, git, patches, and commands stay inside the real workspace tree.</p></div></div><div class="workspace-scene reveal"><div class="workspace-scene__art" style={`--art-image: url("${base}images/workspace/workspace-atlas.svg")`}><div class="workspace-canvas" data-three-scene="workspace" data-asset={`${base}models/gxx-core-module.glb`}></div><div class="scene-tag mono">WORKSPACE / LIVE MAP <span class="pulse-dot"></span></div><div class="scene-boundary mono">ROOT / my-project<br /><span>boundary locked</span></div></div><div class="workspace-tree mono"><div class="tree-label">CONTEXT DISCOVERED</div><div class="tree-row tree-row--active"><span>⌄</span><b>my-project/</b><small>ROOT</small></div><div class="tree-row"><span>›</span><span>src/</span><small>FILES</small></div><div class="tree-row"><span>›</span><span>test/</span><small>FILES</small></div><div class="tree-row"><span>›</span><span>internal/</span><small>FILES</small></div><div class="tree-row"><span>·</span><span>go.mod</span><small>READ</small></div><div class="tree-row"><span>·</span><span>.git/</span><small>INSPECT</small></div><div class="tree-row tree-row--blocked"><span>×</span><span>../outside</span><small>BLOCKED</small></div></div></div><div class="context-path"><span>PROMPT</span><i></i><span>DISCOVER</span><i></i><span>SELECT</span><i></i><span>MODEL CONTEXT</span></div></div></section>

			<section class="security-section section-space section-grid" id="security" aria-labelledby="security-title"><div class="shell security-grid"><div class="security-copy reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 05 — SECRET AWARE</div><p class="eyebrow">PATH CHECK / EVERY TOOL</p><h2 id="security-title">Close to the code.<br /><em>Far from the secrets.</em></h2><p>gxx omits or refuses sensitive paths such as `.env`, credentials, private keys, secret files, `.ssh`, and `.git`. It is workspace-aware, not an OS sandbox.</p><div class="security-status"><span class="status-lock">×</span><div><b>ACCESS → BLOCKED</b><span class="mono">sensitive path detected</span></div></div></div><div class="security-visual reveal"><div class="security-visual__art" style={`--art-image: url("${base}images/security/security-boundary.svg")`}><div class="security-canvas" data-three-scene="security" data-asset={`${base}models/gxx-core-module.glb`}></div><div class="security-visual__label mono">BOUNDARY / SENSITIVE PATHS</div></div><div class="security-flow mono"><span>REQUEST</span><i>↓</i><span>PATH CHECK</span><i>↓</i><span class="flow-blocked">SECRET / BLOCK</span></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="provider-section section-space" id="providers" aria-labelledby="provider-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 06 — MODEL LAYER</div><div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN PROVIDERS / YOUR ACCOUNT</p><h2 id="provider-title">Bring the model<br /><em>you already use.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">gxx supports OpenAI and Claude accounts. The active provider, model, effort, context, and permission are visible in the session line.</p></div><div class="provider-console reveal" data-provider-console><div class="provider-console__nav" role="tablist" aria-label="providers"><button class="provider-tab is-active" data-provider="openai">OPENAI <span>01</span></button><button class="provider-tab" data-provider="claude">CLAUDE <span>02</span></button></div><div class="provider-console__body"><div class="provider-mark" data-provider-mark>OPENAI<span>●</span></div><div class="provider-details"><div><span class="mono">PROVIDER</span><b data-provider-name>OpenAI</b></div><div><span class="mono">MODEL</span><b data-provider-model>gpt-5.6-sol</b></div><div><span class="mono">LOGIN</span><b data-provider-login>API key / ChatGPT</b></div><div><span class="mono">SESSION</span><b data-provider-session>context · effort · fast</b></div></div><div class="provider-visual"><div class="provider-scan"></div><div class="provider-ring"></div><span class="mono">MODEL ROUTE<br /><em data-provider-route>OPENAI / CODEX</em></span></div></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="flow-section section-space section-grid" id="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-title"><div class="flow-section__art" aria-hidden="true" style={`--art-image: url("${base}images/agent/agent-context.svg")`}></div><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading section-heading--split reveal"><div><div class="section-index mono">/ 07 — GXX FLOW</div><p class="eyebrow">FROM WORDS TO WORKING TREE</p><h2 id="flow-title">A decision<br /><em>with a trail.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">The agent loop stays legible: prompt, relevant context, model turn, decision, file or shell action, result.</p></div><div class="flow-rail reveal" data-flow-rail><div class="flow-node is-active"><span>01</span><b>PROMPT</b><small>natural language</small></div><i></i><div class="flow-node"><span>02</span><b>CONTEXT</b><small>workspace files</small></div><i></i><div class="flow-node"><span>03</span><b>MODEL</b><small>provider + effort</small></div><i></i><div class="flow-node"><span>04</span><b>DECISION</b><small>permission gate</small></div><i></i><div class="flow-node"><span>05</span><b>FILE / SHELL</b><small>approved action</small></div><i></i><div class="flow-node"><span>06</span><b>RESULT</b><small>visible output</small></div></div><div class="flow-caption mono"><span data-flow-caption>INPUT RECEIVED</span><span>SCROLL TO TRACE</span></div></div></section>

			<section class="observability-section section-space" id="observability" aria-labelledby="observability-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 08 — OBSERVABILITY</div><div><p class="eyebrow">KNOW WHAT THE AGENT IS DOING</p><h2 id="observability-title">No black-box<br /><em>status line.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">Session state is part of the interface: model, permission, effort, context window, tokens, and estimated USD cost.</p></div><div class="telemetry-board reveal"><div class="telemetry-board__header"><span class="mono">SESSION / OBSERVABILITY</span><span class="board-live"><b></b> LIVE UI / NO SESSION CONNECTED</span></div><div class="telemetry-grid"><div class="telemetry-card telemetry-card--wide"><div class="telemetry-card__head"><span>CONTEXT WINDOW</span><span class="mono">MODEL-NATIVE</span></div><div class="context-gauge"><div class="gauge-ring"><span>—</span></div><div class="gauge-copy"><b>272k / 1m</b><span>available context labels vary by model</span></div></div><div class="gauge-line"><span>USED</span><i><b></b></i><span>SESSION DATA CONNECTS IN CLI</span></div></div><div class="telemetry-card"><div class="telemetry-card__head"><span>TOKEN USAGE</span><span class="mono">INPUT / OUTPUT</span></div><div class="empty-chart empty-chart--bars"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><div class="empty-chart__label mono">AWAITING SESSION DATA</div></div></div><div class="telemetry-card"><div class="telemetry-card__head"><span>ESTIMATED COST</span><span class="mono">USD / TURN</span></div><div class="empty-chart empty-chart--line"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 130" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 110H400M0 75H400M0 40H400"/><path d="M0 106C42 106 48 92 80 94S124 60 152 78s38-28 66-23 52 33 72 8 56-16 110-42" stroke-dasharray="4 10"/></svg><div class="empty-chart__label mono">BENCHMARK DATA NOT PUBLISHED</div></div></div></div><div class="telemetry-board__footer mono"><span>RATE SOURCE / OFFICIAL PROVIDER PAGES</span><span>VALUES APPEAR AFTER A REAL TURN</span><span>NO FABRICATED METRICS</span></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="benchmark-section section-space section-grid" id="benchmarks" aria-labelledby="benchmark-title"><div class="shell"><div class="benchmark-header reveal"><div><div class="section-index mono">/ 09 — MEASURED, WHEN MEASURED</div><p class="eyebrow">PERFORMANCE, MEASURED.</p><h2 id="benchmark-title">A dashboard<br /><em>waiting for runs.</em></h2></div><div class="benchmark-state"><span class="benchmark-state__dot"></span><b>BENCHMARK DATA<br />NOT PUBLISHED YET.</b><small>UI is ready for reproducible measurements.</small></div></div><div class="benchmark-dashboard reveal"><div class="benchmark-dashboard__top"><span class="mono">BENCHMARK FRAMEWORK / EMPTY STATE</span><span class="mono">RUN ID —</span></div><div class="benchmark-charts"><div class="chart-panel"><div class="chart-panel__head"><b>LATENCY GRAPH</b><span>REQUEST → RESPONSE</span></div><div class="plot plot--line"><div class="plot-grid"></div><div class="plot-axis plot-axis--y"><span>latency</span><span>—</span><span>—</span><span>—</span></div><div class="plot-axis plot-axis--x"><span>run 01</span><span>run 02</span><span>run 03</span><span>run 04</span></div><div class="plot-empty mono">NO RUNS</div></div></div><div class="chart-panel"><div class="chart-panel__head"><b>TOKEN USAGE</b><span>INPUT / OUTPUT / TOTAL</span></div><div class="plot plot--bars"><div class="plot-grid"></div><div class="bar-placeholder"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="plot-empty mono">NO SESSION EXPORT</div></div></div><div class="chart-panel"><div class="chart-panel__head"><b>COST PER TURN</b><span>P50 / P95 / AVG</span></div><div class="plot plot--distribution"><div class="distribution-line"></div><div class="distribution-empty mono">AWAITING REPRODUCIBLE MEASUREMENTS</div></div></div></div><div class="benchmark-dashboard__legend mono"><span><i class="legend-cyan"></i>OBSERVED</span><span><i class="legend-violet"></i>BASELINE</span><span><i class="legend-dash"></i>NOT AVAILABLE</span></div></div><div class="benchmark-method reveal"><div class="benchmark-method__intro"><p class="eyebrow">HOW WE MEASURE</p><h3>Make the claim<br />traceable.</h3><p>No numbers until the setup, prompt, repository, model, and run policy are recorded.</p></div><div class="method-pipeline"><div class="method-pipeline__line"><span class="is-active">TEST</span><i></i><span>RUN</span><i></i><span>COLLECT</span><i></i><span>AGGREGATE</span><i></i><span>VISUALIZE</span></div><div class="method-specs"><div><b>HARDWARE</b><span>record before run</span></div><div><b>OS / GXX VERSION</b><span>pin the environment</span></div><div><b>MODEL / PROMPT</b><span>same input, stated</span></div><div><b>REPOSITORY / RUNS</b><span>size + cold/warm</span></div><div><b>ACCOUNTING</b><span>latency + tokens + cost</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="comparison-section section-space" id="comparison" aria-labelledby="comparison-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading section-heading--split reveal"><div><div class="section-index mono">/ 10 — OBJECTIVE SURFACE</div><p class="eyebrow">COMPARISON WITHOUT THE HYPE</p><h2 id="comparison-title">Properties,<br /><em>not promises.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">The comparison stays within what the repository documents. A dash means the project does not publish a comparable claim.</p></div><div class="comparison-table reveal" role="table" aria-label="gxx documented properties"><div class="comparison-row comparison-row--head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">CAPABILITY</span><b role="columnheader">GXX</b><span role="columnheader">BASELINE</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>terminal-native</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>one-folder scope</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>ask / plan / agent</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>permission modes</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>sensitive path checks</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>OpenAI / Claude</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>cost visibility</span><b>ESTIMATE</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row" role="row"><span>SSH / one-shot / skills</span><b>YES</b><span>—</span></div><div class="comparison-row comparison-row--note" role="row"><span>startup / latency / memory</span><b>NOT PUBLISHED</b><span>—</span></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="skills-section section-space section-grid" id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-title"><div class="shell skills-grid"><div class="skills-visual reveal"><div class="skills-canvas-wrap"><div class="skills-canvas" data-three-scene="skills" data-asset={`${base}models/gxx-core-module.glb`}></div><div class="skills-canvas__label mono">MODULE GRAPH / SKILL.MD</div></div><div class="skills-nodes mono"><span>review</span><span>deploy</span><span>debug</span><span>docs</span></div></div><div class="skills-copy reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 11 — PROGRESSIVE INSTRUCTIONS</div><p class="eyebrow">AGENT SKILLS / SKILL.MD</p><h2 id="skills-title">Load the right<br /><em>knowledge.</em></h2><p>Skills live in `.agents/skills`, `.gxx/skills`, or the user config directory. gxx sends a compact catalog each turn and loads a matching `SKILL.md` when needed.</p><div class="skills-list"><div><span>01</span><b>DISCOVER</b><small>catalog at the start of a turn</small></div><div><span>02</span><b>READ</b><small>load the matching skill body</small></div><div><span>03</span><b>APPLY</b><small>keep safety and permissions in charge</small></div></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}skills/`}>Read the skills docs <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>

			<section class="eco-section section-space" id="eco" aria-labelledby="eco-title"><div class="shell eco-grid"><div class="eco-copy reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 12 — ECO MODE</div><p class="eyebrow">LESS FILLER / SAME MODEL</p><h2 id="eco-title">Compress the noise.<br /><em>Keep the signal.</em></h2><p><code>/eco</code> is session-only input slimming. It removes filler and keeps code, paths, URLs, and identifiers. It never changes the selected model.</p><div class="eco-levels mono"><span class="is-active">LITE</span><span>FULL</span><span>ULTRA</span></div></div><div class="eco-demo reveal"><div class="eco-demo__head mono"><span>REQUEST TRANSFORM</span><span class="tone-green">/eco full</span></div><div class="eco-line"><b>VERBOSE</b><span>I would like you to please explain what this function does in detail.</span></div><div class="eco-arrow">↓ <span>filler removed / identifiers protected</span></div><div class="eco-line eco-line--after"><b>COMPACT</b><span>Explain what function does detail.</span></div><div class="eco-demo__footer mono"><span>MODEL / UNCHANGED</span><span>QUANTITATIVE SAVING / NOT CLAIMED</span></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="cli-section section-space section-grid" id="cli" aria-labelledby="cli-title"><div class="shell cli-grid"><div class="cli-copy reveal"><div class="section-index mono">/ 13 — ONE-SHOT CLI</div><p class="eyebrow">WHEN A REPL IS TOO MUCH</p><h2 id="cli-title">Ask once.<br /><em>Pipe the answer.</em></h2><p>Use `gxx ask` for a single request, JSON output, or stdin. The same workspace and permission rules still apply.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}cli/`}>View CLI docs <span>→</span></a></div><div class="one-shot-terminal reveal"><div class="one-shot-terminal__bar mono"><span>ONE-SHOT / NON-INTERACTIVE</span><span>STDIN READY</span></div><div class="one-shot-terminal__body mono"><div><span class="tone-cyan">$</span> gxx ask <em>"explain this repository"</em></div><div class="one-shot-dim">→ context / workspace root</div><div class="one-shot-dim">→ provider / active account</div><div class="one-shot-answer">This is a workspace-scoped coding agent. It can read the project, inspect git, and — in agent mode — propose or apply changes.</div><div><span class="tone-cyan">$</span> echo <em>"what does main.go do?"</em> | gxx ask</div></div></div></div></section>

