			<section class="install-section section-space section-grid" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title"><div class="shell"><div class="install-header reveal"><div><div class="section-index mono">/ 17 — START HERE</div><p class="eyebrow">INSTALL / CONNECT / OPEN A FOLDER</p><h2 id="install-title">Put gxx<br /><em>in the terminal.</em></h2></div><span class="install-version mono">CURRENT DOCS / v0.0.25</span></div><div class="install-console reveal" data-install-console><div class="install-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="installation platforms"><button class="install-tab is-active" data-install="unix">macOS / LINUX</button><button class="install-tab" data-install="windows">WINDOWS / POWERSHELL</button><button class="install-tab" data-install="source">BUILD FROM SOURCE</button></div><div class="install-command"><div class="install-command__label mono"><span data-install-label>QUICK INSTALL / SHELL</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy={unixInstall} data-copy-label="COPY" data-copied-label="COPIED">COPY</button></div><pre><code data-install-command>{unixInstall}</code></pre><div class="install-follow mono" data-install-follow><span>THEN</span><b>cd your-project</b><span>→</span><b>gxx</b><span>→</span><b>type what you want</b></div></div><div class="install-notes"><span>• OpenAI: API key or ChatGPT login</span><span>• Claude: Pro/Max or token</span><span>• Go 1.27+ for source builds</span><span>• macOS / Linux / Windows</span></div></div></div></section>

			<section class="faq-section section-space" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="shell"><div class="section-heading section-heading--split reveal"><div><div class="section-index mono">/ 18 — FAQ</div><p class="eyebrow">NO HIDDEN SURFACE</p><h2 id="faq-title">Useful answers,<br /><em>plainly stated.</em></h2></div><p class="section-heading__note">The short version of what the repository documents. Read the docs for the full contract.</p></div><div class="faq-list reveal"><details><summary>What is gxx?<span>+</span></summary><p>A Go coding agent CLI that runs inside one project directory. It can list, search, read, inspect git, patch files, and run commands according to the active mode and permissions.</p></details><details><summary>Can it edit files?<span>+</span></summary><p>Agent mode can apply file changes when the permission policy allows it. Ask and Plan are read-only; Ask previews changes and Plan creates a plan before execution.</p></details><details><summary>What happens with .env and keys?<span>+</span></summary><p>Sensitive paths are omitted or refused across file tools, image writes, git inspect, and commands that name them. This is not a promise of OS-level sandboxing.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use Claude or OpenAI?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. The documented providers are OpenAI and Anthropic/Claude. Credentials can come from API keys or supported account login flows described in the docs.</p></details><details><summary>How does cost estimation work?<span>+</span></summary><p>After turns, gxx can show estimated USD based on token usage and rates refreshed from official OpenAI and Anthropic pricing pages. This website does not publish benchmark or session cost data.</p></details><details><summary>What is /eco?<span>+</span></summary><p>A session-only input compressor. Lite, full, and ultra remove filler while keeping code, paths, URLs, and identifiers. The model does not change.</p></details><details><summary>Does it sandbox shell commands?<span>+</span></summary><p>No OS sandbox is claimed. In Ask and Plan, shell tools are disabled. In Agent, shell follows the selected permission mode and commands should be reviewed.</p></details><details><summary>What are skills?<span>+</span></summary><p>Project or personal `SKILL.md` instructions discovered progressively from documented skill directories. Safety, permission, and plan rules stay in charge.</p></details></div></div></section>

